How to create docker file? Create Docker Image? push that to docker hub?
------------
FROM        → Base image
MAINTAINER  → Maintainer information (deprecated)
RUN         → Executes during image creation
CMD         → Executes when container starts

vi Dockerfile-------->create file
	^
    	|
	|
	|
FROM openjdk:17----------->Base image
MAINTAINER Pankaj--------->Maintainer information
RUN echo 'run-1'---------->executes during image creation
RUN echo 'run-2'---------->executes during image creation
CMD echo 'cmd-1'---------->executes when the container starts
CMD echo 'cmd-2'---------->Only the last CMD is considered

build docker image
--------------------
docker build -t pankajsiracademy/image1 .

to run executable jar: 
----------------------
java -jar myapp.jar

CMD vs ENTRYPOINT
------------------
example1: CMD "java -jar app.jar"------------------->can override
example2: ENTRYPOINT ["java","-jar","app.jar"] ----->can't override

COPY---copy file one location to another location
------
COPY target/your-app.jar /usr/app/

ADD------copy file and also extract compress file
-----
ADD target/your-app.jar /usr/app/
ADD <http-url> /usr/app/ (wrong)


WORKDIR
---------
works as cd


Example: WORKDIR /path/to/directory

COPY target/your-app.jar   /usr/app/
WORKDIR /usr/app/
CMD "java -jar your-app.jar"


EXPOSE
-------
used to specify application is running on which PORT number


